 },
 "research_note": "THE PUMPING WORKS' GROUNDS, built by T-3689 for the 1871 scene: the open ground before the works, east of Pine Street between Chicago Avenue and Pearson Street. Kurz's lithograph of the works (Jevne & Almini, 1866-67) shows the engine house standing back from Pine Street and Chicago Avenue across open ground and walks, with no house before it; Greene's stereograph of the works after the fire shows its south and west fronts meeting at the corner turret across an open yard, behind an iron railing on a stone kerb along the street; a photograph of about 1890 shows lawn and trees before it. How far the grounds reach east toward the shore is reconstructed.",
